# .gitkeep
# This file preserves the empty public/images directory in Git version control.
# 
# Purpose:
# - Git does not track empty directories, so this placeholder ensures the
#   images directory exists in the repository for all developers.
# - This directory will hold image assets for the UI layer (icons, logos,
#   backgrounds, etc.) that are served via Express.js static file middleware.
#
# Static asset serving:
# - Images placed in this directory are served at /images/* URLs
# - Configuration: express.static('public') in src/app.js
#
# Feel free to delete this file once actual image assets are added.
